# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Um curso gratuito da IBM sobre informação e computação quântica"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Produtos internos e projeções"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Para nos preparar melhor para explorar as capacidades e limitações dos circuitos quânticos, vamos introduzir alguns conceitos matemáticos adicionais — a saber, o *produto interno* entre vetores (e sua conexão com a norma euclidiana), as noções de *ortogonalidade* e *ortonormalidade* para conjuntos de vetores, e matrizes de *projeção*, que nos permitirão introduzir uma generalização conveniente das medições na base computacional padrão.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Produtos internos {#inner-products}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr "Lembre-se de que quando usamos a notação de Dirac para nos referir a um vetor coluna arbitrário como um ket, como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativamente, se temos em mente algum conjunto de estados clássicos $\\Sigma$ e expressamos um vetor coluna como um ket,\n"
"como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr "então o vetor linha (ou bra) correspondente é a transposta conjugada\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Temos também que o produto de um vetor bra por um vetor ket, vistos como matrizes com uma única linha ou uma única coluna, resulta em um escalar.\n"
"Especificamente, se temos dois vetores coluna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1)$, then\n"
msgstr "de modo que o vetor linha $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ é como na equação $(1)$, então\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr "Alternativamente, se temos dois vetores coluna escritos como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2)$, we find that\n"
msgstr "de modo que $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ é o vetor linha $(2)$, encontramos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b$.\n"
msgstr "onde a última igualdade decorre da observação de que $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ e $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ para estados clássicos $a$ e $b$ satisfazendo $a\\neq b$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"O valor $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ é chamado de *produto interno* entre os vetores $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ e $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Os produtos internos são de extrema importância na informação e computação quântica;\n"
"não conseguiríamos avançar muito na compreensão matemática da informação quântica sem eles.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of vectors.\n"
msgstr "Vamos agora reunir alguns fatos básicos sobre produtos internos de vetores.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr "**Relação com a norma euclidiana.** O produto interno de qualquer vetor\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   consigo mesmo é\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr "   Assim, a norma euclidiana de um vetor pode ser alternativamente expressa como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Observe que a norma euclidiana de um vetor deve ser sempre um número real não negativo.\n"
"   Além disso, a única forma de a norma euclidiana de um vetor ser igual a zero é se todas as entradas forem iguais a zero, ou seja, se o vetor for o vetor nulo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr "   Podemos resumir essas observações da seguinte forma: para todo vetor $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   com $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ se e somente se $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   Essa propriedade do produto interno é às vezes chamada de _definição positiva_.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Simetria conjugada.** Para quaisquer dois vetores\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   e portanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$, $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Linearidade no segundo argumento (e linearidade conjugada no primeiro).**\n"
"Suponha que $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ e $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ são vetores e $\\alpha_1$ e $\\alpha_2$ são números complexos. Se definirmos um novo vetor\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   então\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ou seja, o produto interno é _linear_ no segundo argumento.\n"
"   Isso pode ser verificado pelas fórmulas acima ou simplesmente observando que a multiplicação de matrizes é linear em cada argumento (e especificamente no segundo argumento).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle$, $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we define\n"
msgstr "   Combinando esse fato com a simetria conjugada, concluímos que o produto interno é _conjugado linear_ no primeiro argumento. Isto é, se $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ e $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ são vetores e $\\alpha_1$ e $\\alpha_2$ são números complexos, e definirmos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**A desigualdade de Cauchy–Schwarz.**\n"
"Para qualquer escolha de vetores $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ e $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ com o mesmo número de entradas, temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr "   Essa é uma desigualdade incrivelmente útil, amplamente utilizada na informação quântica (e em muitos outros tópicos de estudo).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr "Conjuntos ortogonais e ortonormais {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr "Dois vetores $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ e $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ são ditos *ortogonais* se seu produto interno é zero:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right angles to each other.\n"
msgstr "Geometricamente, podemos pensar em vetores ortogonais como vetores em ângulo reto entre si.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"Um conjunto de vetores $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ é chamado de *conjunto ortogonal* se todo vetor do conjunto é ortogonal a todos os outros vetores do conjunto.\n"
"Ou seja, esse conjunto é ortogonal se\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k$.\n"
msgstr "para todas as escolhas de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ para as quais $j\\neq k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Um conjunto de vetores $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ é chamado de conjunto *ortonormal* se for um conjunto ortogonal e, além disso, todo vetor do conjunto for um vetor unitário.\n"
"Alternativamente, esse conjunto é ortonormal se tivermos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"
msgstr "para todas as escolhas de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por fim, um conjunto $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ é uma *base ortonormal* se, além de ser um conjunto ortonormal, ele forma uma base.\n"
"Isso é equivalente a $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ser um conjunto ortonormal e $m$ ser igual à dimensão do espaço do qual $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ são extraídos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma$, the set of all standard basis vectors\n"
msgstr "Por exemplo, para qualquer conjunto de estados clássicos $\\Sigma$, o conjunto de todos os vetores da base padrão\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"é uma base ortonormal.\n"
"O conjunto $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ é uma base ortonormal para o espaço de dimensão $2$ correspondente a um único qubit, e a base de Bell $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ é uma base ortonormal para o espaço de dimensão $4$ correspondente a dois qubits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr "Estendendo conjuntos ortonormais a bases ortonormais {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m$.\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponha que $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ são vetores que vivem em um espaço de dimensão $n$, e suponha ainda que $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ é um conjunto ortonormal.\n"
"Conjuntos ortonormais são sempre conjuntos linearmente independentes, portanto esses vetores necessariamente geram um subespaço de dimensão $m$.\n"
"Concluímos disso que $m\\leq n$ porque a dimensão do subespaço gerado por esses vetores não pode ser maior do que a dimensão do espaço inteiro do qual foram extraídos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n$, then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Se for o caso que $m<n$, então sempre é possível escolher $n-m$ vetores adicionais\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ de forma que\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forme uma base ortonormal.\n"
"Um procedimento conhecido como *processo de ortonormalização de Gram–Schmidt* pode ser usado para construir esses vetores.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"
msgstr "Conjuntos ortonormais e matrizes unitárias {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Conjuntos ortonormais de vetores estão intimamente relacionados com matrizes unitárias.\n"
"Uma forma de expressar essa conexão é dizer que as três afirmações a seguir são logicamente equivalentes (ou seja, todas são verdadeiras ou todas são falsas) para qualquer escolha de uma matriz quadrada $U$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr "A matriz $U$ é unitária (isto é, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "As linhas de $U$ formam um conjunto ortonormal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "As colunas de $U$ formam um conjunto ortonormal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Essa equivalência é bastante direta quando pensamos em como funciona a multiplicação de matrizes e a transposta conjugada.\n"
"Suponha, por exemplo, que temos uma matriz $3\\times 3$ como esta:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "A transposta conjugada de $U$ tem o seguinte aspecto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr "Multiplicando as duas matrizes, com a transposta conjugada no lado esquerdo, obtemos esta matriz:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U$,\n"
msgstr "Se formarmos três vetores a partir das colunas de $U$,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr "então podemos expressar o produto acima alternativamente da seguinte forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to the equation $(3)$, we now see that the condition that this matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality of the set $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Referindo-se à equação $(3)$, vemos agora que a condição para que essa matriz seja igual à matriz identidade é equivalente à ortonormalidade do conjunto $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esse argumento se generaliza para matrizes unitárias de qualquer tamanho.\n"
"O fato de que as linhas de uma matriz formam uma base ortonormal se e somente se a matriz é unitária decorre então do fato de que uma matriz é unitária se e somente se sua transposta também é unitária.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dada a equivalência descrita acima, juntamente com o fato de que todo conjunto ortonormal pode ser estendido para formar uma base ortonormal, concluímos o seguinte fato útil:\n"
"Dado qualquer conjunto ortonormal de vetores $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ extraídos de um espaço de dimensão $n$, existe uma matriz unitária $U$ cujas primeiras $m$ colunas são os vetores $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictoricamente, sempre podemos encontrar uma matriz unitária com esta forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui, as últimas $n-m$ colunas são preenchidas com qualquer escolha de vetores $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ que tornem\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ uma base ortonormal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Projeções e medições projetivas {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrizes de projeção {#projection-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two properties:\n"
msgstr "Uma matriz quadrada $\\Pi$ é chamada de *projeção* se satisfaz duas propriedades:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr "Matrizes que satisfazem a primeira condição — isto é, que são iguais à sua própria transposta conjugada — são chamadas de *matrizes hermitianas*, e matrizes que satisfazem a segunda condição — que elevá-las ao quadrado as mantém inalteradas — são chamadas de matrizes *idempotentes*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como uma ressalva, a palavra *projeção* às vezes é usada para se referir a qualquer matriz que satisfaça apenas a segunda condição, mas não necessariamente a primeira, e quando isso acontece o termo *projeção ortogonal* é normalmente usado para se referir às matrizes que satisfazem ambas as propriedades.\n"
"No contexto da informação e computação quântica, porém, os termos *projeção* e *matriz de projeção* se referem mais tipicamente a matrizes que satisfazem ambas as condições.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Um exemplo de projeção é a matriz\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"para qualquer vetor unitário $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Podemos ver que essa matriz é hermitiana da seguinte forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Aqui, para obter a segunda igualdade, usamos a fórmula\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr "que é sempre verdadeira, para quaisquer duas matrizes $A$ e $B$ para as quais o produto $AB$ faz sentido.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ver que a matriz $\\Pi$ em $(4)$ é idempotente, podemos usar a hipótese de que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ é um vetor unitário, de modo que satisfaz $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Assim, temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr "De forma mais geral, se $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ é qualquer conjunto ortonormal de vetores, então a matriz\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"é uma projeção.\n"
"Especificamente, temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "e\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr "onde a ortonormalidade de $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implica a penúltima igualdade.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0$, which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"De fato, isso esgota todas as possibilidades: *toda* projeção $\\Pi$ pode ser escrita na forma $(5)$ para alguma escolha de um conjunto ortonormal $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Tecnicamente falando, a matriz zero $\\Pi=0$, que é uma projeção, é um caso especial.\n"
"Para encaixá-la na forma geral $(5)$ devemos permitir que a soma seja vazia, resultando na matriz zero.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Medições projetivas {#projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"A noção de medição de um sistema quântico é mais geral do que apenas as medições na base padrão.\n"
"*Medições projetivas* são medições descritas por uma coleção de projeções cuja soma é igual à matriz identidade.\n"
"Em símbolos, uma coleção $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ de matrizes de projeção descreve uma medição projetiva se\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, two things happen:\n"
msgstr "Quando essa medição é realizada em um sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ enquanto ele está em algum estado $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, duas coisas acontecem:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, the outcome of the measurement is $k$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Para cada $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, o resultado da medição é $k$ com probabilidade igual a\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Para qualquer resultado $k$ que a medição produza, o estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ se torna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma$, if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Também podemos escolher resultados diferentes de $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ para medições projetivas, se desejarmos.\n"
"De forma mais geral, para qualquer conjunto finito e não vazio $\\Sigma$, se temos uma coleção de matrizes de projeção\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "que satisfaz a condição\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma$, where the rules are the same as before:\n"
msgstr "então essa coleção descreve uma medição projetiva cujos possíveis resultados coincidem com o conjunto $\\Sigma$, onde as regras são as mesmas de antes:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $a\\in\\Sigma$, the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Para cada $a\\in\\Sigma$, o resultado da medição é $a$ com probabilidade igual a\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Para qualquer resultado $a$ que a medição produza, o estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ se torna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por exemplo, as medições na base padrão são equivalentes a medições projetivas, onde $\\Sigma$ é o conjunto de estados clássicos de qualquer sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ sobre o qual estamos falando e nosso conjunto de matrizes de projeção é\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, where\n"
msgstr ""
"Outro exemplo de medição projetiva, desta vez em dois qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, é dado pelo conjunto\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, onde\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr "Se temos múltiplos sistemas que estão conjuntamente em algum estado quântico e uma medição projetiva é realizada em apenas um dos sistemas, a ação é similar ao que tínhamos para as medições na base padrão — e de fato podemos agora descrever essa ação em termos muito mais simples do que antes.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$, while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ser preciso, suponha que temos dois sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ em um estado quântico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, e uma medição projetiva descrita por uma coleção $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ é realizada no sistema $\\mathsf{X}$, enquanto nada é feito em $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Fazer isso é então equivalente a realizar a medição projetiva descrita pela coleção\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"no sistema conjunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Cada resultado de medição $a$ ocorre com probabilidade\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "e condicionado ao resultado $a$ aparecer, o estado do sistema conjunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ se torna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Implementando medições projetivas {#implementing-projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr "Medições projetivas arbitrárias podem ser implementadas usando operações unitárias, medições na base padrão e um sistema auxiliar extra, como será explicado agora.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$. We can easily generalize this discussion to projective measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Suponha que $\\mathsf{X}$ é um sistema e $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ é uma medição projetiva em $\\mathsf{X}$. Podemos facilmente generalizar essa discussão para medições projetivas com diferentes conjuntos de resultados, mas para conveniência e simplicidade assumiremos que o conjunto de possíveis resultados da nossa medição é $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr "Notemos explicitamente que $m$ não é necessariamente igual ao número de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ — vamos deixar $n$ ser o número de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X}$, o que significa que cada matriz $\\Pi_k$ é uma matriz de projeção $n\\times n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr "Como assumimos que $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ representa uma medição projetiva, é necessariamente o caso que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, but to do this using only unitary operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr "Nosso objetivo é realizar um processo que tenha o mesmo efeito que realizar essa medição projetiva em $\\mathsf{X}$, mas fazê-lo usando apenas operações unitárias e medições na base padrão.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Faremos uso de um sistema auxiliar extra $\\mathsf{Y}$ para isso, e especificamente vamos tomar o conjunto de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ como sendo $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, que é o mesmo que o conjunto de resultados da medição projetiva.\n"
"A ideia é que realizaremos uma medição na base padrão em $\\mathsf{Y}$, e interpretaremos o resultado dessa medição como sendo equivalente ao resultado da medição projetiva em $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Precisaremos assumir que $\\mathsf{Y}$ é inicializado em algum estado fixo, que escolheremos como $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Qualquer outra escolha de vetor de estado quântico fixo poderia ser feita para funcionar, mas escolher $\\vert 0\\rangle$ torna a explicação a seguir muito mais simples.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X}$, we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y}$, by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Claro, para que uma medição na base padrão de $\\mathsf{Y}$ nos diga algo sobre $\\mathsf{X}$, precisaremos permitir que $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ interajam de alguma forma antes de medir $\\mathsf{Y}$, realizando uma operação unitária no sistema $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"Primeiro considere esta matriz:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Expressa explicitamente como uma chamada *matriz de blocos*, que é essencialmente uma matriz de matrizes que interpretamos como uma única matriz maior, $M$ tem o seguinte aspecto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros, so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr "Aqui, cada $0$ representa uma matriz $n\\times n$ preenchida inteiramente com zeros, de modo que a matriz inteira $M$ é uma matriz $nm\\times nm$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1$, in which case $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I}$, giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely $0$; unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr "Agora, $M$ certamente não é uma matriz unitária (a menos que $m=1,$ caso em que $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ dando $M = \\mathbb{I}$ nesse caso trivial) porque matrizes unitárias não podem ter nenhuma coluna (ou linha) inteiramente $0;$ matrizes unitárias têm colunas que formam bases ortonormais, e o vetor totalmente nulo não é um vetor unitário.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"No entanto, é o caso que as primeiras $n$ colunas da matriz $M$ são ortonormais, e obtemos isso da hipótese de que $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ é uma medição.\n"
"Para verificar essa afirmação, observe que para cada $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, o vetor formado pela coluna número $j$ de $M$ é o seguinte:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0$. Taking the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr "Observe que aqui estamos numerando as colunas a partir da coluna $0$. Calculando o produto interno da coluna $i$ com a coluna $j$ quando $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, obtemos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "que é o que precisávamos mostrar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr "Assim, como as primeiras $n$ colunas da matriz $M$ são ortonormais, podemos substituir todas as entradas zero restantes por alguma outra escolha de entradas de números complexos de modo que a matriz inteira seja unitária.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, we can compute suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr "Se tivermos as matrizes $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, podemos calcular as matrizes adequadas para preencher os blocos marcados com $\\fbox{?}$ na equação — usando o processo de Gram–Schmidt — mas não importa especificamente quais são essas matrizes para fins desta discussão.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X}$, we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, podemos descrever o processo de medição: primeiro realizamos $U$ no sistema conjunto $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ e depois medimos $\\mathsf{Y}$ com respeito a uma medição na base padrão.\n"
"Para um estado arbitrário $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ de $\\mathsf{X}$, obtemos o estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"onde a primeira igualdade decorre do fato de que $U$ e $M$ coincidem em suas primeiras $n$ colunas.\n"
"Quando realizamos uma medição projetiva em $\\mathsf{Y}$, obtemos cada resultado $k$ com probabilidade\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "caso em que o estado de $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ se torna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and $\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Assim, $\\mathsf{Y}$ armazena uma cópia do resultado da medição e $\\mathsf{X}$ muda exatamente como mudaria se a medição projetiva descrita por $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ tivesse sido realizada diretamente em $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
